  "s": "<i>Violence by Design</i> is a printed supplement to <i>The Funambulist</i> #29, published as prison architecture competitions surge + \u201cpenitentiary innovation\u201d takes fashionable urgency across Ivy League departments. Reform elaborates the typology, reinforcing the logic of punitive justice. Prison is not an architecture of detainment but of production \u2014 breaking down the person to create the inmate through a series of dehumanizing protocols \u2014 engineered to supply the underclass on which state infrastructure, war + profit depend. Artworks, case studies + essays trace the seemingly benign design decisions that fix crime, innocence, weapon, defense, authority + victim as categories, + implicate the formal + spatial practices that continue to optimize + sustain them \u2014 ending with a call-to-action to boycott any future participation.",
